<title>UK: BP Q3 replacement net pre-exeps 650 mln stg.</title>
<headline>BP Q3 replacement net pre-exeps 650 mln stg.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Three months to September 30</p>
<p>			   (million stg unless stated)</p>
<p> Shr (pence, replacemt) 11.6		   vs 9.6</p>
<p> Shr (pence, historic)  13.2		   vs 3.3</p>
<p> Dividend (pence)	 5.0		    vs 4.0</p>
<p>Replacement cost net</p>
<p> before exceps	    650		    vs 532</p>
<p>Historic cost net</p>
<p> after exceps	     741		    vs 183</p>
<p>NOTE - Analysts' forecasts on replacement cost profits were in a range of 600 to 675 million stg.  </p>
<p>Replacement cost</p>
<p>    operating	     1,038		  vs 996</p>
<p> Exceptional charge     49		     vs 254 charge</p>
<p> Stockholding gain	129		    vs 100 loss</p>
<p> Interest paid	    86		     vs 115 paid</p>
<p> Pretax		     1,032		  vs 433</p>
<p> Tax			  298		    vs 280</p>
<p>Post-excep replacement cost profit</p>
<p>				612		    vs 283</p>
<p>Average North Sea oil price ($/barrel)</p>
<p>				20.20		  vs $16.40</p>
<p>Breakdown of replacement operating profits per sector</p>
<p> - Exploration and production	  761    vs 527</p>
<p> - Refining and marketing		151    vs 161</p>
<p> - Chemicals				 130    vs 225</p>
<p> - Other business/corporate loss	 4    vs 11 loss</p>
<p> Pay date		   February 3, 1997</p>
<p>Div  registration date November 19</p>
<p> Ex-div date		November  11</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
</text>
